export const legalCrawl = {"privacy":{"title":"Privacy Policy","paragraphs":["Privacy Policy - Bizuply","Read Bizuply's Privacy Policy, including how we collect, use, store, protect, and share user and business data.","Privacy Center","Privacy Policy","This Privacy Policy explains how BizUply collects, stores, uses, and protects personal and business information across the platform.","Last updated:","August 9, 2026","Policy Overview","Quickly navigate between the sections on privacy, data, security, user rights, and legal terms.","Privacy Contact","Last Updated","Introduction","Scope and Applicability","Definitions","Data We Collect","How We Use Your Data","Data Sharing","Google Workspace API Data","Cookies","Data Retention","User Rights","Refunds and Payments","Limitation of Liability","Data Location","Policy Updates","Legal Compliance","Legal Disclaimer","Governing Law","Contact and Data Protection Officer","Final Provision","1. Introduction","This Privacy Policy explains how BizUply , privately owned and operated under the laws of the United States, collects, stores, uses, and protects the personal information of its users and business customers (“Users,” “Businesses,” or “you”). By using the BizUply platform, you agree to the terms described in this document.","Bizuply LLC is a limited liability company formed in Delaware, United States. It provides business-management software, customer communication, and AI features when those features are used. No street address was verified, so none is stated.","This Privacy Policy applies to all of our products, services, websites, and applications (the “Platform”) and describes in detail how we process data, what information we collect, and what rights you have with respect to your information.","By accessing or using our Platform, you acknowledge that you have read and understood this Privacy Policy. If you do not agree, please do not use BizUply or any of its services.","2. Scope and Applicability","This Privacy Policy applies to all users, including businesses, employees, administrators, affiliates, and website visitors who interact with BizUply in any manner, whether through desktop, mobile applications, API integrations, or third-party add-ons.","This policy describes how personal and non-personal information is handled. It does not state that the company complies with any particular privacy statute. A privacy law applies only when its own conditions are met. No compliance audit was completed.","This policy does not apply to third-party services, links, or integrations that are not owned or operated by BizUply. We encourage you to review their privacy policies before engaging with them.","3. Definitions","“BizUply” – Bizuply LLC, a limited liability company formed in Delaware, United States. Its Delaware file number, registered office, and any street address were not supplied and are not stated.","“The Platform” – includes all BizUply products, websites, systems, servers, applications, APIs, AI modules, CRM dashboards, automation tools, and related software infrastructure.","“User” – any natural or legal person who uses BizUply's services, including business owners, employees, customers, or website visitors.","“Personal Information” – data that identifies or can reasonably identify an individual, including but not limited to name, email, phone number, address, payment details, business profile data, and digital identifiers such as IP addresses or cookies.","“Third Parties” – external entities engaged by BizUply for hosting, payment processing, analytics, or communication purposes, subject to binding confidentiality and data protection agreements.","4. Data We Collect","BizUply collects both personal and non-personal data necessary to provide, improve, and secure its services. Data collection may occur directly from you, automatically through your device, or from verified business integrations.","4.1. Personal Data You Provide","Full name, email, and phone number","Business name, registration number, and address","Payment and billing information","Encrypted login credentials","Communications, reviews, and feedback submitted through the Platform","4.2. Data Collected Automatically","IP address and approximate geographic location","Device type, browser version, and operating system","Session activity, interaction history, and timestamps","Cookies and tracking pixels for analytics and performance","4.3. Business and Analytical Data","Customer records and appointments","Business messages and chat logs","AI analysis of performance metrics and recommendations","Aggregated insights generated from anonymized usage data","5. How We Use Your Data","BizUply uses the information collected solely for legitimate business purposes related to operating and improving its Platform. We do not sell or rent personal data under any circumstances.","To provide and maintain our services and customer accounts","To process payments, invoices, and billing cycles","To improve product performance, UX, and AI accuracy — excluding user data received through Google Workspace APIs, as set out in Section 7","To send service updates, notifications, or marketing offers","To ensure compliance with legal and regulatory requirements","To prevent fraud, misuse, or unauthorized access","To support customer service and resolve technical issues","To analyze user behavior for statistical and security purposes","The product review did not establish a written security protocol or compliance with a privacy statute. No such compliance is claimed.","6. Data Sharing and Third Parties","BizUply does not sell or trade personal data. It may share limited information with a provider only where that is needed to operate the platform, to meet a legal duty, or to provide the service. No security certification is claimed.","6.1. Authorized Service Providers","We may share data with carefully selected third-party service providers who assist us with:","Application hosting on Railway, the public site on Vercel, the application database on MongoDB, and Redis for cache and queues. The storage region is not recorded in the product repository.","Platform subscription checkout through Lemon Squeezy. Stripe is used for some merchant-store payments. PayPal is used for some store-order confirmations.","Email through Resend. Phone through Twilio when that service is enabled.","Cloudflare Turnstile loads only on a screen that has a site key. This entry does not claim a separate analytics product.","AI features through OpenAI when a key is configured. This entry does not state whether that provider trains on the content.","Signed confidentiality agreements with these providers were not found in the product repository. A provider may use the information for the service it actually provides.","6.2. Legal Requirements","We may disclose information to law enforcement, government agencies, or legal advisors if required to comply with applicable laws, court orders, or to protect our rights, security, or property, including fraud prevention and dispute resolution.","6.3. Business Transfers","In the event of a merger, acquisition, reorganization, or asset sale, personal data may be transferred to the acquiring entity, provided that the same data protection obligations continue to apply.","8. Cookies and Tracking Technologies","The marketing homepage and the other platform pages load the Meta Pixel only when advertising cookies are allowed. A previously saved value of all is that same advertising permission and is not treated as permission for any other purpose. A missing cookie, the value essential, or a refusal of advertising cookies does not load the pixel. Refusing advertising cookies revokes measurement at once, so further pixel events are not sent, and deletes the measurement cookies this site can delete. If the pixel was already loaded, it is stopped without reloading the page. That refusal does not delete information already received by Meta. The choice stays for 180 days across platform pages and return visits. Cookie settings in the footer, and the same control on the privacy page, reopen the choice. Published customer sites do not load this pixel. Necessary cookies stay on: bizuply_lang for language (365 days), bizuply_tracking for this choice (180 days), bizuply_session as a sign-in hint (up to 365 days when remember-me is on), and the httpOnly refreshToken that keeps a signed-in session (up to 365 days when the session is persistent). No analytics product is installed. No separate non-essential functionality cookie is used.","8.1. Types of Cookies Used","Necessary: bizuply_lang, bizuply_tracking, bizuply_session, and refreshToken. They operate the site, language, this choice, and sign-in, and they stay on.","Analytics: no measurement tool is installed. The category is not in use and has no switch.","Advertising: the Meta Pixel, identifier 1427327632368128, loads only when advertising cookies are allowed, including a previously saved value of all. It can set _fbp and _fbc. This policy does not state a retention period for those Meta cookies.","Functionality: no non-essential functionality cookie is used. Language and sign-in remain necessary cookies.","8.2. Managing Cookies","Users may disable cookies through their browser settings. However, disabling essential cookies may affect functionality or access to certain system features.","BizUply does not respond to browser “Do Not Track” signals. For more information, contact us at support@bizuply.com .","9. Data Retention and Security","BizUply keeps personal and business data to operate the service, to meet a legal duty, and to prevent misuse or fraud. A general process that deletes or anonymizes every record when it is no longer needed was not found in the product. This policy does not state a fixed retention period.","The public site is served over HTTPS. Encryption at rest, firewalls, intrusion detection, and two-factor authentication were not found in the product review and are not claimed. No online system is free of risk. By using BizUply, you acknowledge the inherent risk of transmitting data over the internet.","A written security-incident procedure with a fixed notice time was not found. Where a law that applies requires notice, that law sets the duty.","10. User Rights","Where a privacy law that covers the person grants one of the following rights, the person may send a request to support@bizuply.com. This list is not a statement that any one privacy statute applies to every user.","The right to access personal data stored by BizUply","The right to correct or update inaccurate information","The right to request deletion (“the right to be forgotten”)","The right to receive a copy of personal data (“data portability”)","The right to object to processing or marketing use","Requests must be submitted in writing to support@bizuply.com . BizUply may verify the requester's identity. A response within 30 business days is not an implemented process. The deadline, if any, is the one required by a law that covers the request.","11. Refunds, Payments, and Legal Waiver","All payments, subscriptions, and service fees paid to BizUply are final and non-refundable under any circumstances, including but not limited to account closure, user dissatisfaction, technical issues, downtime, or business suspension.","By using BizUply, the user expressly agrees and acknowledges that:","No refund, credit, or compensation will be granted for any reason whatsoever.","The user waives any right to claim damages, initiate legal proceedings, or demand monetary relief against BizUply, its owners, employees, partners, or affiliates.","BizUply shall not be liable for any indirect, consequential, or incidental losses, including loss of profits, loss of data, or reputational harm.","The user acknowledges full understanding that use of the BizUply platform is entirely at their own discretion and risk.","No oral or written communication overrides the payment terms above, except a mandatory consumer right that this contract cannot waive. The governing law and courts are the Delaware clause in the terms, sections 1.6 and 14.","12. Limitation of Liability","BizUply provides its services “as is” and “as available.” We make no warranty as to continuous operation, accuracy, completeness, or fitness for any purpose.","To the maximum extent permitted by law, BizUply and its affiliates disclaim all liability for any direct, indirect, incidental, consequential, or punitive damages arising from the use of, or inability to use, the Platform.","In any event, BizUply's total liability shall not exceed the amount paid by the user in the thirty (30) days preceding the event giving rise to the claim.","13. Data Location and International Transfers","The product repository does not record a storage region. This policy does not state that personal or business data is stored in one named place. MongoDB, Railway, and the other providers named in the service may process information where they operate.","The repository does not show that storage or transfer is limited to the United States. A provider used by the service may process information where it operates. No standard contractual clause or equivalent-security agreement is claimed.","Using BizUply does not mean that a user's information is subject only to United States law. A mandatory privacy law that covers that user still applies.","14. Policy Updates and Notices","BizUply reserves the right to change, update, or amend this Privacy Policy at any time, at its sole discretion. The latest version will be published on our official website at www.bizuply.com/privacy .","Material changes will be communicated by email or through in-platform notifications where relevant. Continued use of the Platform after such updates constitutes full acceptance of the revised policy.","Users are responsible for reviewing this policy periodically to stay informed of any changes.","15. Legal Compliance and Cooperation","Bizuply LLC is formed in Delaware, United States. The company provides records when a law that applies to the request requires it. This sentence does not state that a compliance program was audited.","We may retain or disclose certain records if required by subpoena, court order, or governmental request, provided that such disclosure complies with United States law and due process requirements.","BizUply is committed to preventing illegal activity, fraud, money laundering, or misuse of its systems. Any suspected violation will be reported to the relevant authorities.","16. Legal Disclaimer and No Liability","The user expressly acknowledges that use of the BizUply platform, its services, and related materials is entirely at their own risk. All content and data are provided “as is” without warranty, express or implied, including but not limited to fitness for a particular purpose, merchantability, accuracy, or reliability.","BizUply, its owners, affiliates, employees, contractors, and partners shall not be liable for any direct, indirect, special, consequential, punitive, or incidental damages arising from the use of, or inability to use, the Platform.","This includes, without limitation, loss of profits, data, goodwill, business disruption, or third-party claims.","The user hereby releases and waives any right to initiate legal proceedings, arbitration, or class action against BizUply on any cause related to the use of the service, fees, or data handling.","The waiver above is the company's position only to the extent the mandatory law that covers the user allows it. It is not enforceable in every country, and it does not remove a right that law does not allow this contract to remove. The terms, sections 1.6 and 14, state the governing law and courts.","17. Governing Law and Jurisdiction","This Privacy Policy and a dispute arising from it are governed by the laws of the State of Delaware and applicable United States federal law, without regard to conflict-of-laws rules that would select another state's law. This does not displace a privacy right that the mandatory law of the person's country does not allow this policy to waive.","The state courts and federal courts in Delaware are the forum, except where a mandatory law gives the person a court that this policy cannot take away.","Sections 1.6 and 14 of the terms and this section state the same Delaware law and the same Delaware courts. The thirty-day negotiation in the terms does not delay urgent relief or a right that mandatory law does not allow the contract to limit.","18. Contact Details and Data Protection Officer","If you have any questions, concerns, or requests regarding this Privacy Policy or your personal data, please contact:","BizUply – Data Protection Office","Email: support@bizuply.com","General support: support@bizuply.com","Formation: Delaware, United States. Street address: not verified.","No data-protection officer was identified in the records supplied for this draft. Privacy requests go to support@bizuply.com. Appointment of a DPO, an EU representative, or a UK representative is not claimed.","19. Final Provision","By accessing or using the BizUply platform, you confirm that you have read, understood, and agreed to all the terms set out in this Privacy Policy. You further acknowledge that this policy constitutes the complete and exclusive statement of the understanding between you and BizUply regarding privacy, and supersedes any prior agreement or representation.","If any part of this policy is deemed unenforceable, the remaining provisions shall continue in full force and effect to the maximum extent permitted by law.","Use of BizUply is agreement to this policy, except a right that mandatory law does not allow the policy to waive."]},"terms":{"title":"Terms of Service","paragraphs":["General","Definitions","Services Offered","Registration & Use","Privacy & Data Protection","User-Generated Content","Payments & Refunds","Limitation of Liability","Force Majeure","Intellectual Property","Accessibility","Changes & Termination","Waiver of Claims","Governing Law","Contact Details","Terms of Service - Bizuply","Read Bizuply's Terms of Service, including use of the platform, payments, privacy, user content, limitations of liability, and dispute resolution.","Legal Center","Terms of Service","Please read these terms carefully before using BizUply's website, app, platform, tools, and services.","Last updated: October 14, 2025","Terms overview","Quick navigation between the main legal sections.","Contact","1. General","1.1. The BizUply website and/or mobile application, hereinafter: “the Company,” “BizUply,” “the Site,” “the System,” or “the App,” operate as a Software-as-a-Service (SaaS) platform intended for professional business management, customer communication, appointment scheduling, collaboration, and automation. The platform connects service providers and customers in order to streamline day-to-day operations and improve digital business efficiency.","1.2. Use of the Site, the App, and the System is subject to these Terms of Use, as well as any applicable law and regulation in the United States. Accessing or using BizUply's services constitutes your full and binding consent to comply with all provisions of this Agreement. If you do not agree to these terms, you must not use the Site, the App, or any of the Company's services.","1.3. Bizuply will give an existing customer appropriate prior notice of a material change to these terms before that change takes effect, except when mandatory law requires the change to take effect sooner. This notice does not delay a change that mandatory law requires, and it does not waive a right that the mandatory law of the customer's country does not allow this contract to waive. A non-material update may be posted on the Site. Continued use after a non-material update is posted is acceptance of that update. Continued use does not by itself make a material change binding on an existing customer before the prior notice in this section.","1.4. These terms are written in English and may from time to time be translated for convenience into other languages. In the event of any conflict or inconsistency between translations, the English version shall prevail .","1.5. These terms are drafted in the masculine form for grammatical convenience only and apply equally to all genders, individuals, and entities.","1.6. Bizuply LLC is a limited liability company formed in Delaware, United States. These terms, the privacy policy, and any dispute arising out of or related to the platform or these terms are governed by the laws of the State of Delaware and applicable United States federal law, without regard to conflict-of-laws rules that would select another state's law. This choice does not displace a consumer, privacy, or accessibility right that the mandatory law of the customer's country does not allow a contract to waive. The Delaware file number and registered office are not stated because they were not supplied.","1.7. Users accessing BizUply from outside the United States acknowledge that the platform is operated from within the jurisdiction of the United States and agree that the collection, processing, and storage of their data are subject to the data protection laws and standards of the United States, including any applicable international framework. This acknowledgment does not waive a privacy or consumer right that the mandatory law of the user's country does not allow a contract to waive.","2. Definitions","For the purposes of this Agreement, the following definitions shall apply:","“The Company” – BizUply LLC, the operator and owner of the platform, including its affiliates, employees, partners, and contractors. “The Site” / “The App” – BizUply's digital system, including all websites, domains, databases, APIs, code, infrastructure, interfaces, and related digital assets owned or managed by BizUply. “The User” – any person, professional, business, organization, or other legal entity that accesses or uses the services for business management, communication, or collaboration purposes. “Service Provider” / “Business” – any registered business or independent professional using the platform to create a business profile, manage appointments, customers, tasks, or communication through BizUply. “Customer” – any person or entity that interacts with a business or service provider through the BizUply platform. “The Services” – all features and functions provided by BizUply, including but not limited to CRM tools, messaging, appointment scheduling, automation, AI-driven insights, analytics, reputation management, collaboration tools, reviews, ratings, and business-page creation. “Content” – any data, media, or material submitted, uploaded, transmitted, or displayed on the platform, including text, images, videos, logos, reviews, reports, analytics, or other user-generated material. “Agreement” – this Terms of Use document, which constitutes a legally binding agreement between the User and BizUply. A Business Customer is a registered business buying the service for that business. An Individual Business User is a person buying the service to run or to start a business. A Consumer is a person buying outside a business. A person who buys the service to start a business may still be a consumer under the law of that person's country, and these labels do not decide that question. A Partner or Affiliate is a participant in the partner program. A SaaS Subscriber is a customer on a paid plan or a trial. The partner program's price, commission, renewal, and attribution are the ones shown at purchase. This sentence does not change those rates. Nothing in these terms promises income or profit.","3. Services Offered","3.1. BizUply provides an advanced Software-as-a-Service (SaaS) platform for the comprehensive management of small and medium-sized businesses (“SMBs”). The services are designed to help business owners organize, track, and automate their day-to-day operations through a unified, cloud-based system. Available features include, among others:","Customer relationship management (CRM) for customers and leads","Internal messaging and communication between businesses and customers","Calendar, booking, and appointment-scheduling tools","A verified reviews system and star ratings for customer feedback","Customizable business pages with descriptions, service lists, images, and FAQs","Features for task management, reminders, and follow-ups","Collaboration tools between businesses for shared growth opportunities","An AI-powered business advisor for recommendations and smart automation","Analytics dashboards and performance reports for optimization","3.2. The Company may, from time to time, expand, modify, limit, or discontinue certain features or services. BizUply reserves the right to make such changes at its sole discretion and without prior notice.","3.3. All services, content, and tools provided through the platform are offered “as is” and “as available” , without any warranty of any kind, express or implied, including but not limited to merchantability, fitness for a particular purpose, accuracy, or reliability. The Company does not guarantee continuous availability or error-free operation of the platform.","3.4. Certain services or features may be subject to additional terms, pricing, or subscription tiers. By activating such services, the User agrees to any relevant supplemental terms or pricing structure provided at the time of use.","3.5. Some Bizuply services depend on outside providers, including Meta, WhatsApp, and payment processors. The availability and operation of those services may be affected by outages, limits, and changes that come from those providers. Bizuply does not promise continuous, uninterrupted availability of an outside service. This is subject to Bizuply's contractual commitments and to the law that applies. It does not change a price, a commission, or a partner term.","4. Registration & Use of the System","4.1. To access the full range of BizUply services, users are required to create an account by providing accurate and complete information, including but not limited to their full name, a valid email address, phone number, business name, and payment details where relevant.","4.2. The User agrees to keep their login credentials confidential and is solely responsible for all activity that occurs under their account, whether authorized or not. The Company shall not be liable for any damage, loss, or unauthorized access resulting from failure to maintain proper account security.","4.3. The User agrees to notify the Company immediately of any suspected unauthorized access or security breach related to their account. Failure to do so may result in suspension or termination of access to the platform.","4.4. The Company reserves the right to suspend, restrict, or permanently delete any account that violates these terms, infringes intellectual property rights, distributes harmful or unlawful content, or engages in activity that may harm the integrity of the platform or other users.","4.5. The Company further reserves the right to remove any business, profile, content, or uploaded material that, in its sole discretion, is deemed inappropriate, misleading, fraudulent, offensive, or inconsistent with BizUply's brand values or its legal obligations, without any obligation to provide prior notice or justification.","4.6. Creating multiple or duplicate accounts to abuse trial periods, referral programs, or promotions is strictly prohibited. The Company may terminate or merge such accounts and cancel any related benefits without a refund.","4.7. Upon registration, the User grants BizUply a limited, non-exclusive, worldwide, royalty-free license to store, process, and display the information provided, solely for the purpose of providing and improving the services in accordance with the Company's Privacy Policy .","4.8. The business customer is responsible for making sure there is an appropriate lawful basis to collect personal information, to contact people, to send marketing messages, and to use the Meta and WhatsApp accounts that the customer connects to the platform. Nothing in this paragraph reduces Bizuply's own duties under the law that applies to Bizuply.","5. Privacy & Data Protection","5.1. The Company protects personal information with the administrative, technical, and organizational measures the product actually uses. The GDPR, the CCPA, and the CPRA are named only as laws that may apply when their own conditions are met, including who the customer is and where that customer is. This section does not state that those laws apply to every user, and it does not state that the Company has been found to comply with them.","5.2. In the course of using the platform, the Company may collect, process, and store the following categories of data:","Personally Identifiable Information (PII): such as full name, email address, phone number, business name, billing address, and payment information, as provided during registration or the use of premium features.","Technical data: including IP address, device identifiers, browser type, operating system, connection logs, session duration, geographic location where permitted, and other diagnostic data.","Business data: such as CRM records, appointments, communications, notes, tasks, and statistical usage information generated by the User within the BizUply system.","5.3. The purposes for which data is collected and processed include:","Providing, maintaining, and improving the Company's services","Personalizing the user experience and optimizing system performance","Ensuring legal compliance, preventing fraud, and maintaining security","Sending service-related updates, notices, and offers relevant to the User","Performing analytics to improve the platform's functionality and reliability","5.4. The Company does not sell or rent personal information. Personal data will be shared with third parties only in the following limited circumstances:","With authorized service providers such as secure cloud hosting, analytics, billing, email, or customer support systems, solely for operational purposes and subject to confidentiality obligations.","As required by law, subpoena, or a lawful government request.","In the event of a merger, acquisition, or asset transfer, provided that the receiving entity maintains equivalent privacy protections.","User rights where a law that covers that user grants them","The right to access the personal data collected about them.","The right to correct inaccurate or incomplete personal information.","The right to request deletion (“the right to be forgotten”).","The right to receive a copy of their data (“data portability”).","The right to opt out of the sale or sharing of personal data.","The right to restrict or object to certain types of data processing.","The right to lodge a complaint with a relevant data protection authority or privacy regulator.","5.6. Privacy requests may be sent to support@bizuply.com. The product does not contain a fixed response deadline, and a response within 30 business days is not an implemented process. Any deadline that applies is the one required by a law that actually covers that request.","Cookies & Tracking Technologies","5.7. The Site and the App use cookies and similar technologies for basic functionality, security, and the measurement described in section 5.9. Section 5.9 states which measurement tool loads and on which page.","5.8. Users may disable or restrict cookies through their browser settings; however, as a result, certain features of the platform may not function properly.","5.9. This site does not load Google Analytics, Google Tag Manager, or reCAPTCHA. The Meta Pixel, identifier 1427327632368128, is not loaded on a published customer site. On the marketing homepage and the other platform pages, the pixel loads only when advertising cookies are allowed, including a previously saved value of all. If the cookie is missing, equals essential, or advertising cookies are refused, the pixel does not load. Refusing advertising cookies revokes measurement at once: further pixel events are not sent, the measurement cookies this site can delete are deleted, and, if the pixel was already loaded, it is stopped without reloading the page. Information already received by Meta is not deleted by that refusal. Cookie settings in the footer, and the same control on the privacy page, reopen the choice. The choice stays in a cookie on this browser for 180 days, including when the visitor moves between platform pages and when the visitor returns. A checkout event is sent from registration only when advertising cookies are allowed and measurement has not been revoked. Cloudflare Turnstile loads only on a screen that has a site key configured.","For more information about how BizUply collects, uses, and protects data, please review our detailed Privacy Policy , which forms an integral part of these Terms of Use.","6. User-Generated Content","6.1. Users may upload, post, or share content including text, images, reviews, comments, or business-related data through the platform. All such content remains the sole responsibility of the user who created or uploaded it.","6.2. By submitting any content to the platform, users represent that:","They own or have obtained all rights and licenses necessary to use and share such content.","The content does not infringe the intellectual property, privacy, publicity, or other legal rights of any third party.","The content is not defamatory, fraudulent, obscene, hateful, harassing, discriminatory, or otherwise unlawful.","6.3. The Company reserves the right, but not the obligation, to monitor, edit, or remove any content that violates these terms or applicable law, without prior notice and at its sole discretion.","6.4. By uploading or submitting content to the platform, users grant the Company a worldwide, royalty-free, non-exclusive, perpetual, and irrevocable license to store, reproduce, modify, distribute, and publicly display such content for the purpose of operating, promoting, and improving the services, including marketing and analytical use. This license shall survive the termination of the user's account.","6.5. The Company is not responsible for, and does not endorse, user-generated content. Users acknowledge that they may be exposed to content they consider inappropriate or inaccurate, and they assume all risks associated with such exposure.","7. Payments, Pricing & Refund Policy","⚖️ Legal notice: This section must be read together with Section 13 “Waiver of Claims, Refunds, and Limitation of Actions,” which further clarifies the User's waiver of any right to claim, dispute, or request refunds for any reason.","7.1. Access to a paid BizUply plan requires an active subscription. Platform subscriptions are paid through Lemon Squeezy. Stripe is used for some merchant-store payments, and PayPal is used for some store-order confirmations. A payment is subject to the terms of the processor that handles it.","7.2. Unless otherwise stated, all payments are final and non-refundable . This includes early cancellations, unused service periods, account deactivation, or dissatisfaction with the service. Once a subscription is purchased, it will remain active for the entire purchased period and cannot be shortened, paused, or refunded , even if the User decides to stop using the platform or terminates their account.","7.3. The User acknowledges and agrees that any refund, credit, or adjustment shall be determined solely at the Company's sole discretion . BizUply has no legal or financial obligation to issue refunds under any circumstances. The User expressly waives any right to request chargebacks, open refund claims through payment providers, or demand restitution by any means.","7.4. In cases of account suspension, restriction, or removal due to a violation of these terms, improper use, abusive conduct, or unlawful activity, the Company reserves the right to terminate the User's subscription immediately without prior notice. In such cases, no refund, credit, or compensation will be provided for the remainder of the subscription period.","7.5. The Company may modify, suspend, or discontinue paid features or services at any time and without liability, provided that such actions do not violate active billing obligations under applicable U.S. consumer protection laws.","Trial Periods, Renewals & Cancellations","7.6. New users may be eligible for a free trial period, as indicated on the Site. Upon expiration of the trial period, subscriptions will automatically renew to a paid plan unless cancelled before the renewal date.","7.7. Users may cancel their subscriptions at any time from their account dashboard. Cancellations take effect at the end of the current billing period, and no partial refunds or credits will be provided for the remaining days in the period.","7.8. Users are solely responsible for keeping their billing and payment information up to date. Failed or declined payments may result in temporary suspension or termination of access without a refund.","Price Changes","7.9. The Company reserves the right to change subscription fees, package rates, or service prices at any time, in accordance with applicable U.S. consumer protection laws.","7.10. Any updated pricing will be posted on the Site and communicated to active subscribers by email at least 14 days before renewal. Continued use of the platform after a price change constitutes full acceptance of the new rates.","7.11. If a user does not agree to a price change, they may cancel their subscription before the next billing date to avoid additional charges.","7.12. Sections 7.2, 7.3, 7.4, and 13 do not waive a refund or cancellation right that a mandatory consumer law gives a particular customer. For a consumer in the United States, the Restore Online Shoppers' Confidence Act, 15 U.S.C. § 8403, makes it unlawful to charge for an internet negative-option feature unless the material terms are clearly disclosed before billing information is taken, the consumer gives express informed consent, and a simple mechanism is provided to stop recurring charges. The FTC's 2024 expanded Negative Option Rule, including click-to-cancel, was vacated by the U.S. Court of Appeals for the Eighth Circuit on 8 July 2025, and the FTC restored the pre-2024 rule effective 12 February 2026. That expanded rule is not stated here as a law in force. For a consumer in California, Business and Professions Code § 17602 requires automatic-renewal disclosures, affirmative consent, and cancellation information when that statute applies. For a consumer in the European Union, Directive 2011/83/EU provides a 14-day withdrawal right for a distance contract unless an Article 16 exception applies, including the digital-content exception only when its consent and acknowledgment conditions are met. These laws are not described as applying to every customer. Where one applies, it controls over a contrary no-refund sentence. The no-refund wording above is kept as the company's position for customers to whom no such mandatory right applies.","8. Limitation of Liability","8.1. The services provided by BizUply are offered solely “as is” and “as available” . The Company makes no representations or warranties of any kind, express or implied, including but not limited to warranties of merchantability, fitness for a particular purpose, accuracy, reliability, or non-infringement.","8.2. The Company does not warrant that the platform or its services will be uninterrupted, secure, error-free, or continuously available. Access may be affected by factors beyond the Company's reasonable control, including but not limited to maintenance, updates, third-party system failures, or network disruptions.","8.3. To the maximum extent permitted by law, the Company, its officers, employees, partners, and affiliates shall not be liable for any indirect, incidental, special, consequential, punitive, or exemplary damages arising out of or related to:","The use of, or inability to use, the platform or its services;","Any loss of data, corruption, or unauthorized access;","Errors, omissions, or inaccuracies in any displayed content;","Business interruption, loss of profits, or damage to reputation;","Any act, omission, or negligence of third-party service providers.","8.4. In any event, the Company's total aggregate liability, whether in contract, tort, negligence, or otherwise, shall not exceed the total amount paid by the User to the Company during the thirty (30) days preceding the event giving rise to the claim.","8.5. The User acknowledges that BizUply does not provide legal, financial, or tax advice. Any business decision made through the platform is the sole responsibility of the User.","8.6. The Company shall not be liable for disruptions or damages caused by external factors, including but not limited to cyberattacks, hardware or software failures, internet service provider outages, data-center failures, or third-party integrations.","8.7. Certain jurisdictions do not allow the exclusion or limitation of certain damages or liability. In such cases, the Company's liability shall be limited to the minimum extent permitted by applicable law.","9. Force Majeure","9.1. The Company shall not be liable or deemed to be in breach of these terms for any delay, failure, or interruption in performance resulting from causes beyond its reasonable control, including but not limited to acts of God, natural disasters, war, terrorism, riots, strikes, labor disputes, governmental actions, cyberattacks, data breaches, power or internet outages, pandemics, or other emergencies.","9.2. During any force majeure period, the Company's obligations shall be suspended to the extent that performance is prevented or delayed. The Company will make reasonable efforts to resume normal operations after the event has ceased.","9.3. Users acknowledge that such events may cause temporary disruptions to platform access or delays in service delivery, and the Company shall not be liable for this.","10. Intellectual Property","10.1. All intellectual property rights in and related to the platform, including but not limited to software code, architecture, algorithms, databases, user interfaces, designs, text, graphics, trademarks, trade names, service marks, videos, and other content, collectively “BizUply Materials,” are and shall remain the sole property of BizUply or its licensors.","10.2. Except as expressly permitted in writing by the Company, no part of the Site, the App, or the System may be copied, modified, distributed, republished, displayed, transmitted, reverse-engineered, decompiled, or otherwise exploited for any commercial or non-commercial purpose.","10.3. Users are granted a limited, non-exclusive, non-transferable, and revocable license to access and use the platform solely for lawful business purposes, in accordance with these terms.","10.4. All third-party logos, brands, and trademarks appearing within the platform are the property of their respective owners. Their inclusion does not imply endorsement or affiliation.","10.5. Businesses or users who upload or provide content to the platform represent that they own or have obtained all rights, licenses, and permissions necessary for such content, and that it does not infringe the intellectual property or proprietary rights of any third party.","10.6. Any feedback, ideas, or suggestions provided by users to the Company may be used freely by BizUply for product improvement, without obligation or compensation to the User.","11. Accessibility","11.1. The Company wants the platform to be usable by people with disabilities. A conformance audit against WCAG 2.1 Level AA has not been completed, and this draft does not claim that conformance. On 6 November 2026, Hebrew and English public pages were checked at desktop width and at 390 pixels for language, direction, and horizontal overflow, and one contrast correction was made. A full screen-reader pass and a review of every template were not done. A person who needs help can write to support@bizuply.com. A coordinator's name and telephone number were not supplied. The ADA, the European Accessibility Act, the UK Equality Act 2010, and Israel's accessibility regulations and Standard 5568 may apply only when their own conditions are met. This section does not decide that any of them applies.","11.2. The Company works continuously to improve accessibility features and the user experience across all supported devices and browsers.","11.3. If users encounter any accessibility barriers or need assistance, they may contact support@bizuply.com . The Company will make reasonable efforts to review and address the request within a commercially reasonable time frame, subject to technological feasibility.","11.4. BizUply may offer accessibility accommodations such as text enlargement, color-contrast changes, screen-reader compatibility, and simplified navigation modes where relevant.","12. Changes, Termination & Suspension","12.1. The Company may modify, update, or amend these Terms of Use, the Privacy Policy, or any other platform policy. Updated versions will be posted on the Site with an updated “Last updated” date. A material change to these terms is governed by section 1.3.","12.2. Continued use of the platform after a non-material update is posted is acceptance of that update. A material change applies to an existing customer only after the prior notice in section 1.3, except when mandatory law requires an earlier effective date.","12.3. The Company may suspend, restrict, or terminate the User's account or access to the platform, in whole or in part, without prior notice and without liability, if:","The User violates these terms or any applicable law.","The User engages in activity that may harm the platform, its users, or the Company's reputation.","The User fails to make required payments or engages in fraud.","Technical or security issues require immediate suspension.","12.4. Upon termination, all rights granted to the User under these terms shall immediately cease, and the User must discontinue all access to and use of the platform. Any outstanding payment obligation shall survive termination.","12.5. The Company reserves the right to discontinue or modify the platform or any of its features at any time, temporarily or permanently, without prior notice.","12.6. When the relationship ends, the customer's ability to export, receive, or delete the customer's information follows these terms, the data-processing annex, and the law that applies. These terms do not state a specific retention, deletion, or export period, because no such period was verified as an operating process.","13. Waiver of Claims, Refunds & Limitation of Actions","13.1. The User hereby irrevocably waives, to the maximum extent permitted by applicable law, any claim, demand, legal proceeding, refund request, chargeback, or cause of action against BizUply, its parent company, subsidiaries, affiliates, officers, directors, employees, agents, and licensors, arising out of or related to the use of the platform, the services, payments, billing, or any other engagement with the Company.","13.2. The User acknowledges and agrees that all payments made to BizUply are final and non-refundable . No refund, credit, or compensation will be provided for early cancellation, dissatisfaction, downtime, technical issues, or discontinuation of use of the services. Any refund or credit, in whole or in part, as a matter of goodwill, shall be determined solely at the Company's sole discretion , and the Company shall have no obligation of any kind to provide such refunds under any circumstances.","13.3. The User expressly and irrevocably waives the right to initiate, participate in, or assist in any class action, collective action, representative proceeding, or group claim against BizUply, its affiliates, or representatives. Any dispute or claim shall be handled on an individual basis only .","13.4. This waiver includes, without limitation, any claim for negligence, breach of contract, misrepresentation, loss of profits, business interruption, damage to reputation, or any other alleged direct, indirect, or consequential damage. The User fully understands and agrees that by using the platform they release BizUply from any liability or responsibility for financial or business outcomes arising from the use or misuse of the services.","13.5. To the extent permitted by law, any claim or cause of action arising out of or related to these terms must be filed within one (1) year after the claim arose; otherwise, it shall be permanently barred. After this period, the User shall have no right to take any legal or financial action against the Company.","13.6. The waivers in this section 13, including the class or collective action waiver, and the arbitration clause in section 14, are not represented as enforceable against every customer in every country. They operate only to the extent the law that mandatorily protects that customer allows them. A customer keeps any right that law does not permit this contract to remove. The waiver text above is kept as the company's position where that law allows it.","14. Governing Law & Dispute Resolution","14.1. The same Delaware law governs these terms and the privacy policy.","14.2. The parties will first try to resolve a dispute by good-faith negotiation for thirty (30) days. That period does not delay a request for urgent injunctive or equitable relief, and it does not delay or waive a right that the mandatory law of the customer's country does not allow this contract to limit.","14.3. After that period, the state courts and federal courts located in Delaware are the exclusive forum, except where a mandatory law of the customer's country gives that customer a court that this contract cannot take away. For a dispute that such a law does not reserve to another court, the customer consents to personal jurisdiction in those Delaware courts.","14.4. The Company may seek injunctive or equitable relief in those Delaware courts to protect its intellectual property or confidential information. Section 14.2 means this request need not wait until the negotiation period ends.","14.5. A dispute is brought in the Delaware courts described above, except where mandatory law reserves another court. No other state law and no arbitral seat is selected.","15. Contact Details","For questions, inquiries, legal notices, or privacy-related requests, please contact BizUply at:","Email: support@bizuply.com","Business address: A street address is not stated. None was verified. The company is Bizuply LLC, formed in Delaware, United States. The Delaware file number and registered office were not supplied.","The Company strives to respond to all inquiries within a reasonable time frame, typically within 5–10 business days .","These terms constitute the entire agreement between the User and BizUply regarding the use of the platform, and supersede any prior oral or written understanding. If any provision is found unenforceable, the remaining provisions shall remain in full force and effect.","Last updated","October 2025"]}};
